"Diyu": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Jin_Chushi._Yama_the_Fifth_King_of_Hell%2C_late_12_century._Metmuseum.jpg/1920px-Jin_Chushi._Yama_the_Fifth_King_of_Hell%2C_late_12_century._Metmuseum.jpg","title":"A king of hell holds court","desc":"One of a set of hanging scrolls of the Ten Kings of Hell, painted in ink and colour on silk by Jin Chushi before 1195 and now in the Metropolitan Museum of Art; the file's uploader identifies this king as Yama. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jin_Chushi._Yama_the_Fifth_King_of_Hell,_late_12_century._Metmuseum.jpg","alt":"A tall silk scroll in a gold brocade mount, read from top to bottom. A red-robed king in a winged official's cap sits scowling behind a plain wooden desk while a clerk in green, in a black scholar's cap, leans in holding out an open document. Below them blue-skinned demons drag a barefoot man in white towards a large round mirror on a stand, and at the foot of the scroll an armoured demon swings two swords among snakes and thorn trees where small figures are being tormented."},
