"Neolithic_Europe": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Expansion_of_farming_in_western_Eurasia%2C_9600%E2%80%934000_BCE.png/1920px-Expansion_of_farming_in_western_Eurasia%2C_9600%E2%80%934000_BCE.png","title":"The expansion of farming in western Eurasia, 9600–4000 BCE","desc":"A relief map from the Levant to Ireland, coloured in bands that spread outwards from a dark red core in the Fertile Crescent through orange in the Balkans to green across central Europe, blue along the Mediterranean and yellow in Britain, Ireland and Denmark, with dashed arrows tracing the routes and a calendar year against each band. Gronenborn, Horejs, Börner and Ober, CC BY 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Expansion_of_farming_in_western_Eurasia,_9600%E2%80%934000_BCE.png","alt":"A relief map from the Levant to Ireland, coloured in bands that spread outwards from a dark red core in the Fertile Crescent through orange in the Balkans to green across central Europe, blue along the Mediterranean and yellow in Britain, Ireland and Denmark, with dashed arrows tracing the routes and a calendar year against each band"},
