"Stirrup_jar": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Mycenaean_-_Stirrup_Jar_-_Walters_482084_-_Three_Quarter_Top.jpg","title":"Stirrup jar","desc":"This jar is named for its handle, which resembles a stirrup. Originally created in Crete in the 16th century BCE, the stirrup jar was extremely popular throughout the Aegean region for both storage and transport and became the most characteristic Mycenaean vessel type. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mycenaean_-_Stirrup_Jar_-_Walters_482084_-_Three_Quarter_Top.jpg","alt":"Mycenaean - Stirrup Jar - Three Quarter Top"},
