"Stratum": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Stratum.JPG/1920px-Stratum.JPG","title":"Stratum","desc":"Goldenville Strata exposed at a local quarry. Bedford, Nova Scotia, Canada. The Goldenville strata is made up of thick layers of ocean sediments that were laid down during the Middle Cambrian period and which were subsequently pushed up onto land. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stratum.JPG","alt":"Goldenville Strata exposed at a local quarry"},
